      "content": "It's not just about being tired. It's about the dignity of the arc. A great play doesn't just keep going until the actors are old and the stage is rotting; it ends when the story is complete. There's a certain beauty in knowing when the masterpiece is finished, instead of waiting for the paint to crack and peel. Don't you think there's something more profound about leaving while the vision is still clear?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
